{
  "id": "window_knob_coreg",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [
    "affective_state_core"
  ],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "area": "retina",
  "description": "WINDOW-AS-A-KNOB (block 241000). Deepens block 239000's arousal/window-of-tolerance/co-regulation dyad into its genuine prior-art delta: the window of tolerance rendered as a FORMAL, settable, inspectable window-WIDTH knob (width = hi-lo = 2*half_width, a settable node attr) with a measured onset-vs-width dose-response, and a BIDIRECTIONAL dyad. Rides the REAL affective_state_core AffectiveState.arousal and reuses 239000's WindowOfTolerance node + the same sd_blend leaky-EMA pull form (x <- x + k*(target-x)). NEW vs 239000: (1) the infant's arousal PULLS the caregiver's (wk_caregiver_pull_by_infant -- mutual entrainment); (2) the caregiver has its OWN dynamic arousal + window + regulated flag that flips when its arousal leaves its OWN [lo,hi] (wk_caregiver_dysreg_onset -- co-dysregulation); (3) the infant's co-regulation pull is GATED on the caregiver being regulated (wk_infant_coreg_pull), so a NARROW-window caregiver is pulled into co-dysregulation and FAILS to co-regulate while a WIDE-window one stays regulated and succeeds -- the SAME width knob governs single-agent tolerance AND two-agent co-regulation capacity. Concedes co-regulation-the-mechanism as prior art (coupled-oscillator dyads; active-inference CPC; arousal-caregiver robot); claims ONLY the settable window-width knob + the single<->two-agent unification. 'Kids do well if they can' (Greene): dysregulation is a STATE, never a badness -- NO reward/punishment. self_load_only, default-OFF; NO Rust, NO new Term.",
  "microtheory": {
    "name": "window_of_tolerance_as_a_settable_knob",
    "description": "The window of tolerance is a settable WIDTH (hi-lo). The stressor magnitude at which an agent dysregulates is a monotonic function of that width. In a bidirectional dyad the caregiver's OWN width sets how much of the infant's distress it can absorb before being pulled into co-dysregulation -- one knob, single-agent tolerance and two-agent co-regulation capacity."
  },
